theory.intro:
A **sector** is the region between two radii and the arc joining them. Its area is the fraction $\dfrac{\theta}{2\pi}$ of the circle area $\pi r^{2}$, which simplifies to $A = \tfrac{1}{2}r^{2}\theta$. Convert degrees to radians first.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\usetikzlibrary{angles, quotes}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (3,0);
\coordinate (Q) at (-1.5,2.598);
\fill[gray!35] (O) -- (P) arc (0:120:3) -- cycle;
\draw (O) circle (3);
\draw[thick] (O) -- (P) node[midway, below] {$r$};
\draw[thick] (O) -- (Q) node[midway, above left] {$r$};
\draw[thick] (P) arc (0:120:3);
\pic[draw, "$\theta$", angle radius=0.7cm, angle eccentricity=1.5] {angle=P--O--Q};
\node at (60:2.1) {$A$};
\node[below left] at (O) {$O$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

